   "note": "Leaf 3 is an advertiser page under the running head 'BROOKLYN DIRECTORY ADVERTISER' -- and it is the PUBLISHER'S OWN self-advertisement, which confirms both houses at once: 'PUBLISHING OFFICE OF THE BROOKLYN DIRECTORY, POST-OFFICE BUILDING, MONTAGUE STREET ... J. LAIN & CO., Publishers', and facing it 'NEW YORK STEAM PRINTING HOUSE. WYNKOOP, HALLENBECK & THOMAS, Book, Job and Newspaper Printers, No. 113 FULTON STREET' -- the same printing house as 1864BPL. It also carries a canvassing-fraud warning: 'No money to be paid on account of this Directory, without evidence of authority, signed by J. Lain.'"
